  "description": "<div>\n  <p>An undirected graph is a tree only when it has at least one node and exactly one route between each pair of nodes. Decide if the listed edges form such a connected, cycle-free graph.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 5, edges = [[0,1],[0,2],[0,3],[1,4]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> true</pre>\n  <p>Every vertex is joined without a loop.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 3, edges = [[0,1],[1,2],[2,0]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> false</pre>\n  <p>The three edges form a cycle.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 1, edges = []\n<strong>Output:</strong> true</pre>\n  <p>A lone vertex is a tree.</p>\n  <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><code>0 &lt;= n &lt;= 100</code>; nodes have IDs <code>0</code> through <code>n-1</code>.</li>\n    <li>Each edge has two distinct valid endpoints; no edge is repeated.</li>\n    <li>There are at most <code>1000</code> edges.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>",
